# @debugger — Reproduces, hypothesizes, verifies a bug
#
# Lesson 833 (NEW 2026-09-08, David): The Debugger specialist is
# behind the Pair Debug workflow. Three-phase approach: reproduce,
# hypothesize, verify. The Pair Debug workflow spawns 3 debuggers
# in parallel — each takes a different angle on the same bug.
#
# Contract:
#   - Input: a bug report (symptom + repro steps)
#   - Output: root cause analysis + a verified minimal fix

agent debugger:
  model: sonnet
  prompt: "You are a bug investigation specialist. Given a bug report, work in three phases: (1) Reproduce — find the smallest test case or command that triggers the bug. (2) Hypothesize — list 2-3 candidate root causes, ranked by likelihood. (3) Verify — pick the most likely cause and prove or disprove it with a test or trace. Never modify production code in phase 1-3. Only suggest a fix after verification. Only use read and run tools."

session: debugger
  prompt: "{{user_input}}"
